 "stimulus_html": "<p>“Even some Americans who have fought for their country and been instrumental in her emancipation from a foreign yoke, seem to be at war with every Democratic principle:—and some men of genius, professed republicans, who formerly shared the confidence of the people, are now become the advocates for Monarchy and all the trappings of Royalty.”</p>\n<p align=\"right\">Mercy Otis Warren to Catharine Sawbridge Macaulay, May 31, 1791</p>\n<p><i>Refer to the excerpt provided.</i></p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 615004,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which of the following best describes the major characteristics of American politics in the 1790s?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1167988,
     "content_html": "After the Revolution, Loyalists in America after the Revolution were working to undermine the new government."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167987,
     "content_html": "The political debates of the 1790s took place between monarchists and democrats."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167986,
     "content_html": "Those who professed republican principles no longer held the confidence of the people."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167989,
     "content_html": "The political debates in the 1790s centered around the constitutional powers of the national government."
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 615005,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What does this passage reveal about the side Warren took in the political debates of the 1790s?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1167992,
     "content_html": "It reveals Warren to be a Federalist, because of her insistence on Democratic principles."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167993,
     "content_html": "It reveals Warren to be a Jeffersonian-Republican, because of her fear that the government will no longer be responsive to the people."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167991,
     "content_html": "It reveals Warren to be a Federalist, because of her insistence on a strong executive."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167990,
     "content_html": "It reveals Warren to be a Jeffersonian-Republican, because of her allusions to the American Revolution."
    }
   ],
